1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,083
Vroom vroom! The morning after the party, everyone raced back to the square. Something was jumping!

2
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:12,240
It jumped all night long! Boing, boing, boing! I didn't sleep one bit!

3
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:15,288
A jumping box! Cool! Is it a rocket? I love rockets!

4
00:00:15,638 --> 00:00:17,788
Maybe it's a tiny bunny! Can I hold it? Please?

5
00:00:18,139 --> 00:00:23,335
It's just a box. A loud, shiny box. I hate shiny things.

6
00:00:23,685 --> 00:00:27,354
Don't look at me. I didn't deliver that one. It wasn't on my list.

7
00:00:27,704 --> 00:00:31,203
Then, with a squeak of brakes, the best detective in town arrived.

8
00:00:31,553 --> 00:00:34,988
Inspector Bolt. I heard a boing. Many boings.

9
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:38,644
Big Bertha. It is your gift. You should open it.

10
00:00:38,994 --> 00:00:42,181
Okay! Everybody, count with me! One, two, three!

11
00:00:43,931 --> 00:00:45,844
It's a ball! A shiny red bouncy ball!

12
00:00:46,194 --> 00:00:49,095
The ball bounced so high, it almost touched the clouds.

13
00:00:49,446 --> 00:00:52,809
Whoa! That ball is faster than me! Almost. Not really. Okay, a little.

14
00:00:53,158 --> 00:00:57,204
Look, there's a little note! It says... For Bertha. From a secret friend.

15
00:00:57,554 --> 00:01:00,809
A secret friend? But who? I want to say thank you!

16
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:05,703
A gift with no name. A giver with no face. This is a mystery.

17
00:01:06,053 --> 00:01:10,106
Nobody is in trouble. But everyone will take the Truth Press.

18
00:01:10,456 --> 00:01:13,997
The Truth Press again? My roof still remembers last time!

19
00:01:14,347 --> 00:01:15,414
Procedure.

20
00:01:15,764 --> 00:01:18,482
Me first! Me first! I'm always first! It's kind of my thing.

21
00:01:18,832 --> 00:01:22,203
Turbo. Did you send the secret gift to Big Bertha?

22
00:01:22,553 --> 00:01:25,191
Yes! Totally! It was me! I'm the secret friend! Ta-da!

23
00:01:26,741 --> 00:01:29,898
Turbo, your eyes are getting very, very big.

24
00:01:30,248 --> 00:01:32,584
They're just... excited eyes! Happy birthday eyes!

25
00:01:32,934 --> 00:01:36,049
The Truth Press squeezed, and something fell out of Turbo's trunk!

26
00:01:37,599 --> 00:01:40,337
Okay, okay! It wasn't me. I just wanted a thank you too.

27
00:01:40,687 --> 00:01:42,770
Turbo! You can't take a thank you that isn't yours!

28
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,355
Sorry. I'll keep my banana. And my real eyes.

29
00:01:45,705 --> 00:01:49,353
A banana is not a secret friend. Next! Dash.

30
00:01:49,703 --> 00:01:53,671
I deliver gifts every day. But I didn't send this one. Promise.

31
00:01:54,021 --> 00:01:56,112
The Truth Press came closer and closer...

32
00:01:56,461 --> 00:02:00,024
His eyes stayed small. Dash is telling the truth.

33
00:02:00,374 --> 00:02:03,659
Then why is my roof flat? I have deliveries today!

34
00:02:04,009 --> 00:02:07,465
Procedure. Thank you, Dash. Next! Little Pip.

35
00:02:07,815 --> 00:02:11,269
I wish I sent it! But I only had one sticker, and I gave it to Bertha's card.

36
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,884
The Truth Press squeezed... but once again, it couldn't reach Pip!

37
00:02:16,534 --> 00:02:18,888
Hee hee! It tickles every time! I'm telling the truth!

38
00:02:19,237 --> 00:02:23,845
Turbo, Dash and Pip did not send it. So who is the secret friend?

39
00:02:24,195 --> 00:02:29,176
Not me. Can't be me. I hate shiny things. And presents. And mornings.

40
00:02:29,526 --> 00:02:33,025
Then Inspector Bolt noticed something on the ground near the podium.

41
00:02:33,375 --> 00:02:37,620
Tire tracks. Very big tire tracks. With little zig-zags.

42
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:41,554
These were made last night. By someone big and heavy.

43
00:02:41,904 --> 00:02:44,274
Who has wheels that big? Not me! My wheels are tiny!

44
00:02:44,624 --> 00:02:46,718
Not me! My wheels are skinny and super fast!

45
00:02:47,069 --> 00:02:50,589
Everyone followed the big tracks with their eyes. All the way to...

46
00:02:50,939 --> 00:02:52,176
...Grumpy, the tow truck.

47
00:02:52,526 --> 00:02:56,525
What? Lots of cars have big wheels. Probably.

48
00:02:56,875 --> 00:02:59,734
Grumpy. Would you take the Truth Press, please?

49
00:03:00,083 --> 00:03:03,699
Fine. Ask your question. I'm not worried.

50
00:03:04,049 --> 00:03:06,801
Grumpy. Did you buy a gift for Big Bertha?

51
00:03:07,151 --> 00:03:10,024
No. I did not buy a gift.

52
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:13,831
His eyes are small. True. But one more question.

53
00:03:14,181 --> 00:03:16,954
Grumpy. Did you MAKE a gift for Big Bertha?

54
00:03:18,804 --> 00:03:20,314
Grumpy?! But Grumpy is... grumpy!

55
00:03:20,664 --> 00:03:24,888
He hates shiny things! And that gift was wrapped in shiny gold paper!

56
00:03:25,238 --> 00:03:30,147
Okay. Yes. It was me. I made it in my garage. With a spring.

57
00:03:30,497 --> 00:03:33,209
Grumpy? You made a present? For me? But why?

58
00:03:33,559 --> 00:03:38,636
Every morning, you say good morning to me. Even when I don't say it back.

59
00:03:38,986 --> 00:03:43,799
Nobody else does that. So I wanted to say thank you. Secretly.

60
00:03:44,149 --> 00:03:46,062
Why secretly? It's a wonderful present!

61
00:03:46,412 --> 00:03:52,135
Because I'm Grumpy. Grumpy trucks don't do nice things. It's bad for my name.

62
00:03:52,485 --> 00:03:55,984
Everyone was quiet. Then Inspector Bolt rolled over slowly.

63
00:03:56,334 --> 00:04:00,537
Grumpy. Being kind does not make you less you. It makes you more you.

64
00:04:00,887 --> 00:04:04,130
And remember. Giving feels even better than getting.

65
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:08,502
Hmm. It does feel good. In my engine. Right here.

66
00:04:08,852 --> 00:04:12,627
Thank you, Grumpy! It's the best present ever! Good morning, friend!

67
00:04:12,977 --> 00:04:15,156
...Good morning, Bertha.

68
00:04:15,506 --> 00:04:18,578
And for the very first time, Grumpy said good morning back.

69
00:04:18,928 --> 00:04:21,546
Can we play with the ball now? I'll go first! Obviously!

70
00:04:21,895 --> 00:04:25,372
Let's all play together! I'll deliver the ball to everyone!

71
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:26,993
Catch, Grumpy! Your turn!

72
00:04:27,343 --> 00:04:30,336
Not bad. For a shiny thing.

73
00:04:30,686 --> 00:04:33,993
Case closed. Even the grumpiest heart can give.

74
00:04:34,342 --> 00:04:37,734
But as everyone played, something new was waiting on the podium.

75
00:04:39,484 --> 00:04:42,309
A key? Where did that come from? What does it open?

76
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:45,135
Hmm. Another mystery. Procedure.

77
00:04:45,484 --> 00:04:50,839
What do you think the golden key opens? Tell us in the comments! Inspector Bolt will be back.
